  "coverage": {
    "mode": "explicit-classified",
    "gaps": [
      "No route URL, mount prefix, static root, config key or listen port: omega-javascript, omega-typescript and omega-tsx publish no field on any template, so a call's argument text never reaches the overlay.",
      "A call's receiver is not published either, so app.get and map.get are one fact; every call rule is gated on the artifact importing 'express' and is a module-level claim rather than a receiver-level one.",
      "JS/TS facts carry no resolved external package - the Packs publish 'target'/'module' rather than 'qualifier' - so external_path_matches is unreachable here and no rule uses it.",
      "Handlers are recognised from their TypeScript parameter types; a plain JavaScript (req, res) handler is not distinguishable from any other function.",
      "Runtime middleware ordering, mutation and request execution are runtime state."
    ]
  },
